\title{Class encapsulating a multidimensional raster dataset (experimental)}
\description{
\code{GDALMultiDimRaster} provides an interface for accessing a dataset in the
GDAL Multidimensional Raster Data Model
(\url{https://gdal.org/en/stable/user/multidim_raster_data_model.html}),
such as netCDF, HDF5 or Zarr. An object of class \code{GDALMultiDimRaster}
persists an open connection to the dataset and its root group, and exposes
methods to:
\itemize{
\item retrieve dataset information
\item list the groups and arrays in a group
\item describe the dimensions of a group or an array
\item read the attributes of a group or an array
\item open an array as an object of class \code{\link{GDALMDArray}}
\item create groups, dimensions, arrays and attributes in a dataset opened for
update, or in a new dataset (see \code{\link[=mdim_create]{mdim_create()}}).
}

Groups, arrays and dimensions are addressed by their full path from the
root group, e.g., \code{"/"}, \code{"/group/subgroup"} or \code{"/group/temperature"}. A
path without a leading \code{"/"} is taken from the root. Groups and dimensions
are returned as plain \R lists and data frames. Arrays are opened as
objects of class \code{\link{GDALMDArray}}.

\strong{This class is experimental}. Its interface may change in future releases.
Requires GDAL >= 3.2.

\code{GDALMultiDimRaster} is a C++ class exposed directly to \R (via
\code{RCPP_EXPOSED_CLASS}). Fields and methods of the class are accessed using
the \code{$} operator. \strong{Note that all arguments to class methods are required
and must be given in the order documented.} Naming the arguments is
optional but may be preferred for readability.

In this documentation, "attributes" always means GDAL attributes, i.e.,
metadata stored on groups and arrays in the dataset, not \R object
attributes.
